{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 92,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.92.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is a good thing to give thanks unto Jehovah,\nAnd to sing praises unto thy name, O Most High;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.92.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To show forth thy lovingkindness in the morning,\nAnd thy faithfulness every night,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.92.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "With an instrument of ten strings, and with the psaltery;\nWith a solemn sound upon the harp.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.92.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For thou, Jehovah, hast made me glad through thy work:\nI will triumph in the works of thy hands.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.92.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How great are thy works, O Jehovah!\nThy thoughts are very deep.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.92.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A brutish man knoweth not;\nNeither doth a fool understand this:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.92.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When the wicked spring as the grass,\nAnd when all the workers of iniquity do flourish;\nIt is that they shall be destroyed for ever.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.92.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But thou, O Jehovah, art on high for evermore.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.92.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For, lo, thine enemies, O Jehovah,\nFor, lo, thine enemies shall perish;\nAll the workers of iniquity shall be scattered.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.92.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But my horn hast thou exalted like ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the horn of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the wild-ox:\nI am anointed with fresh oil.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.92.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Mine eye also hath seen ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my desire",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " on mine enemies,\nMine ears have heard ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my desire",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of the evil-doers that rise up against me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.92.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The righteous shall flourish like the palm-tree:\nHe shall grow like a cedar in Lebanon.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.92.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They are planted in the house of Jehovah;\nThey shall flourish in the courts of our God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.92.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They shall still bring forth fruit in old age;\nThey shall be full of sap and green:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.92.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To show that Jehovah is upright;\nHe is my rock, and there is no unrighteousness in him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ],
  "headings": [
    {
      "style": "s1",
      "text": "Praise for Jehovah’s goodness.",
      "before_verse": 1
    },
    {
      "style": "d",
      "text": "A Psalm, a Song for the sabbath day.",
      "before_verse": 1
    }
  ]
}
